{"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"title":"Related Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Autocomplete-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article"],"anchor":"Related-Articles"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Plugins","images":[{"identifier":"Feature-Plugins.jpg","type":"card"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the KeyboardKit plugin engine.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit ships with plugins that can be used to extend the core with additional functionality. Plugins are completely stand-alone and don’t know that KeyboardKit exists, and vice versa.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plugins are used to:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Provide external integrations.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Contain sensitive system API usages.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Contain code that requires certain permissions.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plugins let developers choose whether to use a certain plugin or not, by first considering the permissions and\/or system API usages that this would expose the app to.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"How to use a plugin","anchor":"How-to-use-a-plugin","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can add plugins to an app or keyboard extension when you add KeyboardKit to the project, or at a later time. Some plugins must be linked to the main app target, while others must be linked to the keyboard extension.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Once you have linked a plugin, you must also import it where you’re going to use it. Most plugins just require a single import, since they will be injected at a single, well-defined place.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plugins use basic values to simplify mapping between a plugin and the main library. For instance, the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","isActive":true},{"text":" uses tuples to communicate text and volume data values.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Available Plugins","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Available-Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Below is a list of available plugins that ship with KeyboardKit. You can use the same plugin architecture to implement your own plugins.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Autocomplete","anchor":"Autocomplete","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"KeyboardKitAutocompletePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has advanced ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AutocompleteEngine","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"s that can improve autocomplete for certain locales.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To use this plugin, you must link it to your keyboard extension and import it where you set up KeyboardKit. You can then inject it like this:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import KeyboardKit","import KeyboardKitAutocompletePlugin \/\/ <- 1","","extension PluginLanglotAutocompleteEngine: AutocompleteEngine {} \/\/ <- 2","","class KeyboardController: KeyboardInputViewController {","    ","    ...","    ","    override func viewWillSetupKeyboardKit() {","        super.viewWillSetupKeyboardKit()","        setupKeyboardKit(","            for: .myApp,","            autocompleteEngines: [pluginLanglotAutocompleteEngine]  \/\/ <- 3","        )","    }","}"]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyboardKitAutocompletePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is currently empty, but will be extended with commercial 3rd party engines in the future.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Dictation","anchor":"Dictation","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"KeyboardKitDictationPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" defines a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","type":"reference"},{"text":" that you can use to set up dictation in the app. This engine wraps all the code and imports that require Info.plist permissions, which means that you must only add them if you use this plugin.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To use this plugin, you must link it to the main app target and import it where you set up dictation. You can then inject its engine like this:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import KeyboardKit","import KeyboardKitDictationPlugin \/\/ <- 1","","extension PluginDictationEngine: DictationEngine {} \/\/ <- 2","","struct ContentView: View {","","    var body: some View {","        Text(\"Insert app here :)\")","            .keyboardDictation(withEngine: pluginDictationEngine) \/\/ <- 3","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Dictation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" developer guide for important considerations when setting up dictation for an app and its keyboard extension.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Host-Application","text":"Host Application","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"KeyboardKitHostPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" defines a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplicationResolver","type":"reference"},{"text":" that you can use in the keyboard extension. This resolver wraps all system API usages, which means that it’s only added to your app if you use this plugin.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To use this plugin, you must link it to your keyboard extension and import it where you set up KeyboardKit. You can then inject it like this:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import KeyboardKit","import KeyboardKitHostPlugin \/\/ <- 1","","class KeyboardController: KeyboardInputViewController {","    ","    ...","    ","    override func viewWillSetupKeyboardKit() {","        super.viewWillSetupKeyboardKit()","        setupKeyboardKit(","            for: .myApp,","            hostApplicationResolver: pluginHostApplicationResolver  \/\/ <- 2","        )","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Actions-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AI-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/App-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Autocomplete-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Callouts-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Clipboard-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article","doc:\/\/src.Keyb